 HELP

In Quest, time is important.  That is, actions take real time.  For example,
  walking takes longer than running.
Sentences can be several words long.  For example:  GIVE THE GOLD COIN TO TONY.
Sometimes you can omit words.  For example:  GIVE COIN TO TONY.
Fighting usually requires sentences such as SWING SWORD AT JOHN.
LOOK AT ME tells you how you feel and what you're carrying.
QUIT will get you out of the game permanently.
IT means the last object you referred to.  AGAIN will repeat the last sentence.
To say something, precede it with a quote (").  No trailing quote is required.
  A quoted sentence is heard by everyone else in the room with you.
You can type several sentences on one line.  Just separate them with periods.
You never have to type more than the first five letters of any word.
If your terminal beeps, you're typing too fast.  Wait for your cursor.
See the file QHELP for more information.

